      "claim_id": "c4",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "reasoning": "Passage [6] explicitly recommends converting to journal_mode=DELETE before burning an image onto read-only media.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 6,
          "quote": "Even though it is possible to open a read-only WAL-mode database, it is good practice to convert the database to PRAGMA journal_mode=DELETE prior to burning an SQLite database image onto read-only media."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "reasoning": "Passage [2] states that for transactions larger than about 100 megabytes, traditional rollback journal modes will likely be faster, and notes that the efficiency improvement came in version 3.11.0, implying this was the case before that version.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 2,
          "quote": "For transactions larger than about 100 megabytes, traditional rollback journal modes will likely be faster."
        }
      ]
    },
